---
title: "If your account was rejected"
description: "What a rejection means, how it differs from a request for changes, and what can change the outcome. Also covers accounts described as failing verification."
---

Most accounts that don't pass review the first time are asked to make changes, not rejected. The two look similar in your dashboard and need completely different things from you, so it's worth being certain which one you have.

You may see this described as your verification being rejected. This page covers the **account review** — the check on your business and website. If you're stuck at the identity or document step instead, that's a separate check with a different fix, and [support](mailto:support@creem.io) can tell you which one you're in.

## Which outcome do you have?

| Outcome | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| **Changes requested** | We found something specific that needs fixing. This is not a rejection. Fix it and request a re-review yourself — see the [Re-Review Guide](/merchant-of-record/account-reviews/re-review-guide). |
| **Rejected** | We aren't able to onboard the account as it stands. There's no re-review button for this, and the route is different. |

<Note>
If you can use the **Request re-review** button on **Balance → Payout Account**, you have changes requested, not a rejection. Start with the [Re-Review Guide](/merchant-of-record/account-reviews/re-review-guide).
</Note>

## What changes a rejection

A rejection isn't always final, but it isn't reversed by asking again. What changes the answer is **new information** — something materially different from what we reviewed.

**These count:**

- **The business has changed.** A different product, a different business model, or a different registered entity.
- **Your website now shows something it didn't.** The live product, your legal pages, real pricing — anything that wasn't visible at review.
- **Documentation we didn't have.** Licences, registrations, or supplier and rights agreements relevant to what you sell.
- **We got a fact wrong**, and you can show us the correct one.

**These don't:**

- Asking again
- Explaining what the product was always intended to do
- Confirming you'll comply in future

<Warning>
A repeat request with nothing new attached will reach the same decision. If nothing has changed yet, change it first — then write to us.
</Warning>

## What to send

Write to support with all of the following. A message with these can usually be answered on the first reply; one without them can't.

- **Your store ID** — starts with `sto_`, found in your dashboard settings — and your account email
- **Your website address**, reachable without a login or waitlist
- **What is materially different now**, and when it changed
- **Any supporting documentation**, attached rather than described

Don't send identity documents or card numbers to support. If we need identity verification, we'll send you a secure link.

## While you wait

**Test Mode keeps working.** You can continue building and testing your integration during and after a review — you just can't take live payments until the account is approved.

## What we can't reverse

Some decisions aren't ours to make. Where a business type is prohibited by our payment partners or by card scheme rules, no amount of documentation changes the outcome. We'd rather tell you that plainly than leave you resubmitting — so if that's your situation, we'll say so and we'll say why.

For what we can and can't support, see [Account Reviews](/merchant-of-record/account-reviews/account-reviews).
